A new sampler has been added to the source_sampling.cpp.
See this function:
https://github.com/pyne/pyne/blob/7db8a587c460c986e356bfb10bd42d607f00d477/src/source_sampling.cpp#L90

There are two types of sampler exist and used in the source_sampling.cpp. 
https://github.com/pyne/pyne/blob/7db8a587c460c986e356bfb10bd42d607f00d477/src/source_sampling.cpp#L9
- Old one: sampler for only default/voxel R2S (which you are modifying). They are:
```
if (*mode == 0) {
      sampler = new pyne::Sampler(filename, src_tag_name, e_bounds, false);
    } else if (*mode == 1) {
      sampler = new pyne::Sampler(filename, src_tag_name, e_bounds, true);
    } else if (*mode == 2) {
      std::string bias_tag_name ("biased_source_density");
      sampler = new pyne::Sampler(filename, src_tag_name, e_bounds, bias_tag_name);
    }
```
- sampler for both voxel and sub-voxel R2S:
```
else {
      sampler = new pyne::Sampler(filename, tag_names, e_bounds, *mode);
    }
```

Currently, both of these two types of sampler works, and the old samplers are the default choice of voxel mode. However, as the new sampler works for both voxel and sub-voxel R2S, the old sampler functions could be removed in the future.

It's better to make changes based on the new sampler. By the way, the mode number 3 has been used to represent the sub-voxel analog mode. I suggest you to change the mode number, such as 6.

